// 5:3 on a grid of 20 by 12: three equal bars of 4, and a middle column 6 wide of two equal bars of 6.
// The image's column runs from 448 to 832 pixels of 1280, which is 7 and 13 of 20.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Polyamorish Pride Flag"
  designer "beyond-mogai-pride-flags (Tumblr), signed 'Ap'"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2019-07-26"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20220120235502/https://beyond-mogai-pride-flags.tumblr.com/post/186569055295/polyamorish-pride-flag"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20210630202110/https://www.deviantart.com/nonmonoprideflags/art/Monogamish-Pride-Flag-575041387"
  note "The beyond-mogai-pride-flags Tumblr post 'Polyamorish Pride Flag', as the Wayback Machine held it on 20 January 2022, posted on 26 July 2019 and signed '~ Ap', defines 'Polygamish (polyamourish or polygamorish): a partnership that is mostly polyamorous, but with occasional exceptions', and says 'Based on monogamish flag'. It gives no color meanings, measurements or color values."
  note "It turns NonMonoPrideFlags's monogamish flag inside out: that flag has grey over white with a middle column of blue, red and black; this has blue, black and red bars with a middle column of grey over white. Its colors and column width are its own, not the monogamish flag's, and its bars aren't in the polyamory flag's order."
  note "The post's image is a PNG of 1280 by 768 pixels, 5:3, which this file uses. It draws three equal bars of 256 pixels, and a middle column 384 pixels wide of two equal bars of 384."
  note "The colors are the image's exact pixel values: blue #4848c2, black #1e1e1e, red #c14a4a, grey #7f7f7f and white #ffffff. The image is Tumblr's copy at its largest size, which may have been resized from the upload."
}
palette {
  blue "#4848c2"
  black "#1e1e1e"
  red "#c14a4a"
  grey "#7f7f7f"
  white "#ffffff"
}
proportion hoist=12 fly=20

bars blue black red

panel {
  fly 6
  hoist 12
  bars grey white
}
